      "item": "white chocolate chips",
      "quantity": 0.5,
      "unit": "cup"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "text": "Heat the oven to 350°F. Line baking sheets or prepare them for baking."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "text": "Whisk the melted butter with the brown sugar and white sugar until smooth. Beat in the eggs, then stir in the vanilla extract."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "text": "In a separate bowl, combine the all-purpose flour, baking soda, and salt. Stir the dry mixture into the butter mixture just until no dry flour remains."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "text": "Fold in the crushed pistachios and white chocolate chips."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "text": "Portion the dough onto the prepared baking sheets, leaving space between cookies. Bake until the edges are lightly golden and the centers are set.",
      "timer_minutes": 10
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "text": "Cool the cookies on the baking sheet briefly, then transfer to a rack to cool completely."
    }
  ],
